dialogue story.umbrella.talk
n0 -: A large red umbrella hangs from the fence post, dripping with great dignity. Piper stares at it.
  next n1
n1 piper: It's red. It's enormous. It cannot simply vanish and reappear, and yet. What do you suggest?
  ? Return it to Piper. => r0 | flag:choice.umbrella.return
  ? Hang it where it was found. => r1 | flag:choice.umbrella.hang
  ? Keep it. => r2 | flag:choice.umbrella.keep
r0 piper: Mine. At last. I was starting to take it personally.
  expr happy
r1 piper: Leave it? ...A little red landmark. Yes. I like that.
r2 piper: You'll keep it? That's theft, with excellent manners.
  emote sweat

dialogue story.scarecrow.talk
n0 tilda: Mine has a smile. Smiles scare crows. That is simply known.
  next n1
n1 dorian: Mine is quiet. Quiet is unsettling. I did my research.
  next n2
n2 tilda: Well? Which scarecrow rules the fields?
  ? Tilda's. => r0 | flag:choice.scarecrow.tilda
  ? Dorian's. => r1 | flag:choice.scarecrow.dorian
  ? A tie. => r2 | flag:choice.scarecrow.tie
  ? Ask the crows. => r3 | flag:choice.scarecrow.crows
r0 tilda: Ha! A person of taste. Take this one home. It's the runner-up. It's still excellent.
  expr happy
r1 dorian: ...Oh. Thank you. Take the runner-up. It's very quiet company.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: A tie. You coward. Take one anyway. Both of us will be wounded.
  emote sweat
r3 dorian: The crows? ...Brave. They landed on both. A tie, then. Take this.
  expr thinking

dialogue story.whistler.bram
n0 bram: Hm. I whistle. Don't. Tell. Anyone.
  next n1
n1 bram: ...Well?
  ? Call out a friendly hello. => r0 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.hello
  ? Whistle the wrong note back. => r1 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.back | friend:bram,10
  ? Say nothing. Just listen. => r2 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.listen | friend:bram,10
r0 bram: Hello. Right. Good. Thank you for the normal approach.
r1 bram: You... got the wrong note exactly right. I'm moved and mortified.
  expr embarrassed
r2 bram: You listened. To the whole thing. ...I may whistle again. Quietly.
  expr happy

dialogue story.whistler.marcus
n0 marcus: It's a family tune. One note went wrong in my grandfather's time and we kept it.
  next n1
n1 marcus: ...Well?
  ? Call out a friendly hello. => r0 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.hello
  ? Whistle the wrong note back. => r1 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.back | friend:marcus,10
  ? Say nothing. Just listen. => r2 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.listen | friend:marcus,10
